var quick_start_default = "---\nlayout: article\ntitle: Start with Firewall\ndescription: Create your first Appwrite Firewall rule and see how it affects project API traffic.\ndifficulty: beginner\nreadtime: 5\n---\n\nYou can protect a project API path or block a noisy IP in a few minutes. This quick start creates a deny rule scoped to the project **API**, then points you to traffic monitoring.\n\n# Open Firewall {% #open-firewall %}\n\n1. Sign in to [Appwrite Cloud](https://cloud.appwrite.io).\n2. Open a project.\n3. Open **Firewall** in the sidebar.\n\nIf you do not see **Firewall**, confirm your Console profile includes the feature and that your role can view project navigation.\n\n# Create a deny rule {% #create-a-deny-rule %}\n\n1. Click **Create rule** (or the create action for the **API** tab).\n2. Enter a **Rule name** (for example `Deny staging admin path`).\n3. Leave **Resource type** set to **API** so the rule applies to project API traffic (`/v1/...`).\n4. Under conditions, set:\n   - Attribute: **Path**\n   - Operator: **Starts with**\n   - Value: a path you want to block (for example `/v1/account`)\n5. Set **Action** to **Deny**.\n6. Keep **Priority** at the default (`100`) or choose a lower number so this rule is evaluated earlier.\n7. Leave **Enabled** on.\n8. Review the impact preview in the sidebar, then click **Create rule**.\n\n{% info title=\"Path matching\" %}\nPath conditions use the URL path only. Query strings are ignored. Prefer **starts with** for API prefixes.\n{% /info %}\n\nSee [Create a rule](/docs/products/firewall/create) for functions and sites scopes, rate limits, and redirects.\n\n# Confirm the rule {% #confirm-the-rule %}\n\n1. On the Firewall page, open the **API** tab if it is not already selected.\n2. Find your rule in the list. It should show **Deny** and **Enabled**.\n3. Optionally open the rule to update conditions, priority, scope, or enabled state. See [Update a rule](/docs/products/firewall/update).\n\n# Monitor traffic {% #monitor-traffic %}\n\nThe Firewall overview chart shows overall request volume (**Passed**) plus Firewall outcomes: denied, challenged, rate-limited, and redirected. After traffic hits your deny rule, the denied series should rise when matching API requests arrive.\n\n{% info title=\"Testing from the Console\" %}\nFirewall does not block Console access. To verify a rule, send a request with a client SDK or API key.\n{% /info %}\n\nSee [Monitor traffic](/docs/products/firewall/monitor) for metrics and date ranges, and [Actions](/docs/products/firewall/actions) for what each outcome means.\n";
export { quick_start_default as default };
